; A loop with an unsigned char index unrolled 4 times by clang -O2
; (docs/mair-loops.md, 窄下标回环访问):
;
;   unsigned char i = 0;
;   #pragma clang loop vectorize(disable)
;   for (int k = 0; k < n; k++, i++) a[i] = k;
;
; The unrolled loop starts at k = 0; its copy j stores to a[(k + j) & 255]
; with k = 4m, which SCEV writes as phase j of step 4: 16 * zext i6 {0,+,1},
; 4 + 4 * zext i8 {0,+,4}, 8 + 8 * zext i7 {0,+,2}, 12 + 4 * zext i8 {0,+,4}.
; Each phase starts below its step and visits min(T, 64) elements of stride
; 16 before it comes back to its start, so LPOC summarizes each exactly.
; LocationMerge then interleaves the four (same stride, size and trip count,
; starts 4 apart): one region of 4 * min(T, 64) = min(4T, 256) elements, the
; prefix [0, min(4T, 256)) the copies visit together. The epilogue loop
; starts at the symbolic 4T and stays in its loop.
